<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e7133228","external_id":"fc00704d-6b53-445f-a379-309a3e911067","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"414db40c-01a1-4d79-a4a7-a0d90ebd3d18","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The speed of a vehicle is increasing at a rate of <math alttext=\"7.3\"><mn>7.3</mn></math> meters per second squared. What is this rate, in <strong>miles per minute squared</strong>, rounded to the nearest tenth? <math alttext=\"left parenthesis Use 1 mile  equals 1,609 meters period right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mtext>Use</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>mile</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1,609</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>meters.</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math></p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"43868a4e-f07e-48d9-bf83-e4e9f492d93a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0.3\"><mn>0.3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8850b43a-8e9c-464e-b98d-fa2dc69f1099","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16.3\"><mn>16.3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f91f08f9-feb2-499a-904e-4a02684885d8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"195.8\"><mn>195.8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3b41f722-449f-4dd9-951e-6f6dce6caac2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"220.4\"><mn>220.4</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["8850b43a-8e9c-464e-b98d-fa2dc69f1099"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It's given that the speed of a vehicle is increasing at a rate of <math alttext=\"7.3\"><mn>7.3</mn>\n</math> meters per second squared. It's given to use <math alttext=\"1 mile  equals 1,609 meters\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>mile</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1,609</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>meters</mtext></math>. There are <math alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn>\n</math> seconds in <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> minute; therefore, <math alttext=\"60 squared\"><msup><mn>60</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math> or <math alttext=\"3,600\"><mn>3,600</mn>\n</math> seconds squared is equal to <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> minute squared. It follows that the rate of <math alttext=\"7.3\"><mn>7.3</mn>\n</math> meters per second squared is equivalent to <math alttext=\"left parenthesis StartFraction 7.3 meters Over 1 second squared EndFraction right parenthesis left parenthesis StartFraction 1 mile Over 1,609 meters EndFraction right parenthesis left parenthesis StartFraction 3,600 seconds squared Over 1 minute squared EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>7.3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>meters</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>second&nbsp;squared</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>mile</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1,609</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>meters</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>3,600</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>seconds&nbsp;squared</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>minute&nbsp;squared</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>, or approximately <math alttext=\"16.33 miles per minute squared\"><mn>16.33</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>miles&nbsp;per&nbsp;minute&nbsp;squared</mtext></math>. The rate, <math alttext=\"in miles per minute squared\"><mtext>in&nbsp;miles&nbsp;per&nbsp;minute&nbsp;squared</mtext></math>, rounded to the nearest tenth is <math alttext=\"16.3\"><mn>16.3</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554989,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"e7133228","skill_cd":"Q.A.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","createDate":1743430554989,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"","external_id":"fc00704d-6b53-445f-a379-309a3e911067","primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"414db40c-01a1-4d79-a4a7-a0d90ebd3d18","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The speed of a vehicle is increasing at a rate of <math alttext=\"7.3\"><mn>7.3</mn></math> meters per second squared. What is this rate, in <strong>miles per minute squared</strong>, rounded to the nearest tenth? <math alttext=\"left parenthesis Use 1 mile  equals 1,609 meters period right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mtext>Use</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>mile</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1,609</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>meters.</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math></p>","keys":["8850b43a-8e9c-464e-b98d-fa2dc69f1099"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"43868a4e-f07e-48d9-bf83-e4e9f492d93a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0.3\"><mn>0.3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8850b43a-8e9c-464e-b98d-fa2dc69f1099","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16.3\"><mn>16.3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f91f08f9-feb2-499a-904e-4a02684885d8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"195.8\"><mn>195.8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3b41f722-449f-4dd9-951e-6f6dce6caac2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"220.4\"><mn>220.4</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It's given that the speed of a vehicle is increasing at a rate of <math alttext=\"7.3\"><mn>7.3</mn>\n</math> meters per second squared. It's given to use <math alttext=\"1 mile  equals 1,609 meters\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo