<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for scatterplot" class="sr-only"><ul>
<li>The scatterplot has 7 data points.</li>
<li>The data points are in a linear pattern trending up from left to right.</li>
<li>A line of best fit is shown:<br>
<ul>
<li>The line of best fit slants up from left to right.</li>
<li>The line of best fit passes through the following approximate coordinates:<br>
<ul>
<li>(0 comma 2.5)</li>
<li>(5 comma 3.6)</li>
<li>(10 comma 4.7)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Which of the following is closest to the slope of the line of best fit?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"3431dfb1-11f6-4b22-8d7e-d887f799d87a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 2.45\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2.45</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"eadfdc15-34fc-42c4-9d7d-0b524be08b43","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 0.22\"><mo>-</mo><mn>0.22</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"a760620b-ada6-4232-aa23-bc0428420c70","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0.22\"><mn>0.22</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9f4dc32f-91f2-494b-bb8e-eea4399e2915","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2.45\"><mn>2.45</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["a760620b-ada6-4232-aa23-bc0428420c70"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. A line in the <em>xy</em>-plane that passes through the points <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x 1 comma y 1 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x 2 comma y 2 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math> has a slope of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction y 2 minus y 1 Over x 2 minus x 1 EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>. The line of best fit shown passes through the points with approximate coordinates <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 2.5 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2.5</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 10 comma 4.7 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4.7</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. It follows that the slope of the line of best fit is approximately <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 4.7 minus 2.5 Over 10 minus 0 EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4.7</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2.5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 2.2 Over 10 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>2.2</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0.22"><mn>0.22</mn></math>. Therefore, of the given choices, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0.22"><mn>0.22</mn></math> is closest to the slope of the line of best fit.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is closest to the negative&nbsp;<em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept, not to the slope, of the line of best fit.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is closest to the negative slope, not to the slope, of the line of best fit.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is closest to the&nbsp;<em>y</em>-coordinate of the&nbsp;<em>y</em>-intercept, not to the slope, of the line of best fit.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e9129a5c","external_id":"e798b8cb-3417-44f6-9cd9-077bb0117c35","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"dce5b168-ab57-4cdc-9426-2b307041dcf3","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the given scatterplot, a line of best fit for the data is shown.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 286.56 275.22\" width=\"286.56pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A scatterplot in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from 0 to 10 in increments of 1, with values marked every 2 grid lines. The y axis ranges from 0 to 10 in increments of 1, with values marked every 2 grid lines. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 275.22 \nL 286.56 275.22 \nL 286.56 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 7.2 260.46 \nL 279.36 260.46 \nL 279.36 10.98 \nL 7.2 10.98 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_2\">\n   <g id=\"patch_3\">\n    <path d=\"M 9.200821 268.02 \nL 271.689179 268.02 \nL 271.689179 7.2 \nL 9.200821 7.2 \nz\n\" style=\"fill: