n    <defs>\n     <path d=\"M 0 3 \nC 0.795609 3 1.55874 2.683901 2.12132 2.12132 \nC 2.683901 1.55874 3 0.795609 3 0 \nC 3 -0.795609 2.683901 -1.55874 2.12132 -2.12132 \nC 1.55874 -2.683901 0.795609 -3 0 -3 \nC -0.795609 -3 -1.55874 -2.683901 -2.12132 -2.12132 \nC -2.683901 -1.55874 -3 -0.795609 -3 0 \nC -3 0.795609 -2.683901 1.55874 -2.12132 2.12132 \nC -1.55874 2.683901 -0.795609 3 0 3 \nz\n\" id=\"m6306ee5506\" style=\"stroke:#000000;\"></path>\n    </defs>\n    <g clip-path=\"url(#pd6c2f9f847)\">\n     <use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"62.08272\" xlink:href=\"#m6306ee5506\" y=\"183.030003\"></use>\n     <use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"92.416506\" xlink:href=\"#m6306ee5506\" y=\"187.332668\"></use>\n     <use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"122.750292\" xlink:href=\"#m6306ee5506\" y=\"171.412809\"></use>\n     <use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"142.972815\" xlink:href=\"#m6306ee5506\" y=\"167.540411\"></use>\n     <use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"173.306601\" xlink:href=\"#m6306ee5506\" y=\"169.820823\"></use>\n     <use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"183.417863\" xlink:href=\"#m6306ee5506\" y=\"155.75111\"></use>\n     <use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"223.86291\" xlink:href=\"#m6306ee5506\" y=\"150.028566\"></use>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_2\">\n    <path clip-path=\"url(#pd6c2f9f847)\" d=\"M 41.860197 191.858031 \nL 244.085434 146.689509 \nL 244.085434 146.689509 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"pd6c2f9f847\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"262.488358\" x=\"9.200821\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for scatterplot\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>The scatterplot has 7 data points.</li>\n<li>The data points are in a linear pattern trending up from left to right.</li>\n<li>A line of best fit is shown:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The line of best fit slants up from left to right.</li>\n<li>The line of best fit passes through the following approximate coordinates:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>(0 comma 2.5)</li>\n<li>(5 comma 3.6)</li>\n<li>(10 comma 4.7)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which of the following is closest to the slope of the line of best fit?</p>","keys":["a760620b-ada6-4232-aa23-bc0428420c70"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"3431dfb1-11f6-4b22-8d7e-d887f799d87a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 2.45\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2.45</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"eadfdc15-34fc-42c4-9d7d-0b524be08b43","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 0.22\"><mo>-</mo><mn>0.22</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"a760620b-ada6-4232-aa23-bc0428420c70","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0.22\"><mn>0.22</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9f4dc32f-91f2-494b-bb8e-eea4399e2915","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2.45\"><mn>2.45</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. A line in the <em>xy</em>-plane that passes through the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x 1 comma y 1 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x 2 comma y 2 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math> has a slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction y 2 minus y 1 Over x 2 minus x 1 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>. The line of best fit shown passes through the points with approximate coordinates <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 2.5 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2.5</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 10 comma 4.7 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4.7</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. It follows that the slope of the line of best fit is approximately <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 4.7 minus 2.5 Over 10 minus 0 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4.7</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2.5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 2.2 Over 10 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>2.2</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0.22\"><mn>0.22</mn></math>. Therefore, of the given choices, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0.22\"><mn>0.22</mn></math> is closest to the slope of the line of best fit.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is closest to the negative&nbsp;<em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept, not to the slope, of the line of best fit.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is closest to the negative slope, not to the slope, of the line of best fit.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is closest to the&nbsp;<em>y</em>-coordinate of the&nbsp;<em>y</em>-intercept, not to the slope, of the line of best fit.</p>","externalid":"e798b8cb-3417-44f6-9cd9-077bb0117c35","correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1776362727993,"updateDate":1776362727993}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362727993, 1776362727993),
    ($SATQ$e9841407$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$028058-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Shaquan has 7 red cards and 28 blue cards. What is the ratio of red cards to blue cards that Shaquan has?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">1 to 4</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">4 to 1</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">1 to 7</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">7 to 1</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that Shaquan has 7 red cards and 28 blue cards. Therefore, the ratio of red cards to blue cards that Shaquan has is 7 to 28. This ratio can be reduced by dividing both parts of the ratio by 7, which yields the ratio 1 to 4.<p>Choice B is incorrect. This is the ratio of blue cards to red cards that Shaquan has. Choice C is incorrect and may result from a calculation error when reducing the ratio. Choice D is incorrect. This may result from finding the ratio of blue cards to red cards, or 28 to 7, and then making a calculation error when reducing the ratio.</p></p>
