</math> represent the percentage of <math alttext="300"><mn>300</mn>
</math> that is <math alttext="75"><mn>75</mn>
</math>. This can be written as <math alttext="StartFraction x Over 100 EndFraction left parenthesis 300 right parenthesis equals 75"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mn>300</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn></math>, or <math alttext="3 x equals 75"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mn>3</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>75</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="x equals 25"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>25</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, <math alttext="25 percent sign"><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext="300"><mn>300</mn>
</math> is <math alttext="75"><mn>75</mn>
</math>.</p>
