<p style="text-align: left;">At <math alttext="x equals 25.5"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>25.5</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, which of the following is closest to the <em>y</em>-value predicted by the line of best fit?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"928066ac-61c7-4084-9177-91de02bd5d2d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6.2\"><mn>6.2</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3fab04a9-d202-47a2-a7d4-00d3732f743a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"7.3\"><mn>7.3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f07427a2-751c-4cb2-a5d3-d90dc106b783","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8.2\"><mn>8.2</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3ad597f5-3b9e-4628-bd4f-e1fd0359181a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"9.1\"><mn>9.1</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["f07427a2-751c-4cb2-a5d3-d90dc106b783"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. On the line of best fit, an&nbsp;<em>x</em>-value of <math alttext="25.5"><mn>25.5</mn>
</math> corresponds to a&nbsp;<em>y</em>-value between <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="8.5"><mn>8.5</mn>
</math>. Therefore, at <math alttext="x equals 25.5"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>25.5</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, <math alttext="8.2"><mn>8.2</mn>
</math> is closest to the&nbsp;<em>y</em>-value predicted by the line of best fit.</p>
